 # Transform-based Block Coding
-
-Also called: Block Transform Coding
-
 ## Overview
-Transform-based block coding compresses volumetric data by partitioning it into fixed-size blocks, applying a linear transform to decorrelate values, and entropy coding the resulting coefficients [G]. It differs from global transform methods by enabling localized random access and from predictive coding by exploiting spatial frequency redundancy within blocks rather than inter-voxel differences [G]. It serves as the foundation for methods like [ZFP Block-Based Compression](1504-zfp-block-based-compression.md), [TSDF Block Transform Coding](2548-tsdf-block-transform-coding.md), [JPEG2000](2883-jpeg2000.md), and [Learned Transform Coding](7046-learned-transform-coding.md).
