 ### JPEG2000
-JPEG2000 is a wavelet-based compression standard for still images that serves as the primary benchmark for 2-D coding systems in volumetric data compression. In volume rendering, it is used as a baseline where each 2D layer of a layered image is coded separately using JPEG2000 Part-1, referred to as "Individual layer coding". This approach sets itself apart from 3D volumetric schemes by processing slices independently, which ignores inter-slice correlations and results in visible artifacts at layer boundaries compared to methods that exploit 3D redundancy.
+JPEG2000 is a wavelet-based compression standard for still images that serves as the primary benchmark for 2-D coding systems in volumetric data compression [G]. In volume rendering, it is used as a baseline where each 2D layer of a layered image is coded separately using JPEG2000 Part-1, referred to as "Individual layer coding" [G]. This approach sets itself apart from 3D volumetric schemes by processing slices independently, which ignores inter-slice correlations and results in visible artifacts at layer boundaries compared to methods that exploit 3D redundancy [G].
 
